p.src:
In more than one dimension a region may stretch along one axis and compress along another without changing total volume. For a velocity field $\mathbf V=(V_x,V_y,V_z)$, the relevant local rate is the divergence, $\nabla\cdot\mathbf V
  =
  \frac{\partial V_x}{\partial x}
  +\frac{\partial V_y}{\partial y}
  +\frac{\partial V_z}{\partial z}.$ Positive divergence is local expansion, negative divergence is local contraction, and incompressibility is $\nabla\cdot\mathbf V=0.$ Equal inflow and outflow through a fixed small box is the same local statement as preservation of the volume of a moving small box.

