p.src:
For a smooth Hamiltonian system, the canonical phase-space velocity field has zero divergence: $\sum_i\left(
    \frac{\partial\dot q_i}{\partial q_i}
    +\frac{\partial\dot p_i}{\partial p_i}
  \right)=0.$ Equivalently, Hamiltonian evolution preserves the canonical phase-space volume $dq_1\cdots dq_n\,dp_1\cdots dp_n$.

