The repeated antisymmetric combination deserves a name. For any two functions $F$ and $G$, define their Poisson bracket by $\boxed{
  \{F,G\}
  =
  \sum_i\left(
    \frac{\partial F}{\partial q_i}
    \frac{\partial G}{\partial p_i}
    -
    \frac{\partial F}{\partial p_i}
    \frac{\partial G}{\partial q_i}
  \right).}$

